# The ignore file for `Containerfile.linux.proxy`.
#
# BuildKit looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` beside the Dockerfile before
# it looks for `.dockerignore` at the context root, so this scopes the rules to
# this one image and leaves the root alone -- which matters, because a test in
# `usage/tests/test_all.py` walks the repository root for container files by
# NAME and refuses them there.
#
# WHAT IS NOT IN THIS CONTEXT, AND WHY THAT IS THE POINT
#
#   `server/srv/` in its entirety.  This image proxies bytes: it parses no
#   record, holds no token, opens no store and has no interpreter to do any of
#   it with.  Leaving the package out of the CONTEXT rather than merely out of
#   the COPY list means a later edit cannot put it back without also editing
#   this file, which is a decision somebody has to make on purpose.
#
# The context is the REPOSITORY ROOT, because the image needs `LICENCE`, the
# configuration under `server/oci/nginx/` and `server/oci/entrypoint-proxy.sh`,
# and no one of them is a parent of the others.
*
!/LICENCE
!/server/oci/nginx/**
!/server/oci/entrypoint-proxy.sh
**/__pycache__
